==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|criticise||UK|Irish|Commonwealth}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krey-}}
From {{af|en|critic|-ize}}; first element from {{der|en|grc|κριτικός||of or for judging, able to discern}}, from {{m|grc|κρίσις||decision, judgement}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɹɪtɪsaɪz/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-criticize.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|crit|i|cize}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}} {{tlb|en|ambitransitive}}

# To [[find fault]] (with something).
#: {{syn|en|censure|pick at|Thesaurus:criticize}}
#: {{hypo|en|find fault|shoot down|run down|trash out|fustigate|drub|excoriate}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''criticized''' him for endangering people's lives.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1988-08-13|volume=16|number=5|journal=w:Gay Community News|page=7|author=Elizabeth Pincus|title=1978 Revisited|text=Homophobia is based on '''criticizing''' any any sexual expression outside of procreational sex.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1999-06-18|author=Rod Beaton|title=Astros winning despite obstacles|titleurl=http://www.usatoday.com/sports/baseball/colrod88.htm|journal=w:USA Today
|passage=Since when is it a hanging offense to '''criticize''' someone who's not doing the job he's paid generously to do?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|last=Vassenden|first=Eirik|chapter=Norway: The Province and its Metropolities|
title=The Oxford Critical and Cultural History of Modernist Magazines|volume=3|editors=Peter Brooker; Andrew Thacker|publisher=Oxford University Press|year=2009|ISBN=9780199659586|page=658|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=bvsfioiQ8k8C&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0&lpg=PA658&dq=Scandinavist&pg=PA658#v=onepage&q=Scandinavist&f=false|text=But far from being naïve Scandinavist ideologists, Blix et al. continually '''criticizes''' the utopian Scandinavists' talk of brotherhood and 'one culture', but also—and perhaps most importantly—made cultural separatism and provincialism, particularly in Norway, the object of crass satire.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Paul Hacker (diplomat)|Paul Hacker]]|title=Slovakia on the Road to Independence: An American Diplomat's Eyewitness Account|location=University Park, P.A.|publisher=w:The Pennsylvania State University Press|year=2010|page=52|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/slovakiaonroadto0000hack/page/52/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-271-03623-6|passage=Then Federal Minister of Environment Antonin Vavrougek had strongly '''criticized''' the entire project while working at the Czechoslovak Academy of Sciences in Prague, taking a more limitationist view about the possibilities of generating electricity and a more alarmist view about the effect on drinking water supplies.}}
# To [[evaluate]] (something), [[assess]]ing its [[merit]]s and [[fault]]s.
#: {{syn|en|censure|appraise|judge}}

